{"event_id":"EVT-000042","timestamp_utc":"2026-08-30T21:27:57.808Z","session_id":"SESSION-BATCH-20260830T201120771337Z","run_id":"RUN-IMO-008-20260830T212703754035Z","requirement_id":"IMO-008","event_type":"validator_feedback_possible_reversal","iteration":2,"prior_feedback_history":["Repair the implication logic: do not impose sh:minCount 1 and sh:hasValue nltl:thinFirstYearIce on every ship, because that incorrectly makes every ship applicable and forces the classification. Encode a SHACL alternative in which the branch with iceTypeClassification = nltl:thinFirstYearIce requires iceThickness with a qudt:QuantityValue in unit:M and numericValue between 0.3 and 0.7 inclusive, while the non-applicable branch permits a classification other than thinFirstYearIce (or absent classification if no independent existence requirement applies) without imposing the thickness range. Keep both properties on the supplied ship owner and retain the canonical terms and units."],"current_feedback":"Preserve the prior repair, but fix the non-applicable branch: its SPARQL alternative currently passes a ship that has nltl:iceTypeClassification nltl:thinFirstYearIce because of the EXISTS(thinFirstYearIce) disjunct, allowing the required thickness check to be bypassed. Replace that condition with one that excludes thinFirstYearIce, e.g. FILTER NOT EXISTS { $this nltl:iceTypeClassification nltl:thinFirstYearIce . }, thereby permitting only a different classification or no classification and preventing accidental passes. Keep the applicable branch on the supplied ship owner with the inclusive 0.3\u20130.7 m range and unit:M constraints.","blocking":false,"semantic_attempt_consumed":false}
